--- a/adapters/widesearch/README.md
+++ b/adapters/widesearch/README.md
@@ -237,3 +237,43 @@ This adapter is developed and maintained by [Yizhao Chen](mailto:yic138@ucsd.edu
 ## Acknowledgement
 
 API inference compute for running parity tests is generously supported by [2077AI](https://www.2077ai.com/) (https://www.2077ai.com/).
+
+### Opt-in verifyit verifier
+
+Pass `--verifyit` when generating tasks to run the retained WideSearch scorer
+through verifyit's Script mode in a separate verifier image. The candidate
+workspace is exported as `/workspace`, preserving the native output-file and
+workspace table selection. `evaluate.py`, `metric_utils.py`, and `test.sh` remain
+unchanged; the wrapper retains the native report alongside the primary item F1.
+
+The source harmonizes integer/float dtypes and converts cells to strings, then
+keeps the first row for each composite key before judge alignment and preprocessing. Row credit is the minimum across metric cells;
+item credit sums them, with the original prediction/reference row denominators.
+The pinned Harbor port uses one item column per field/metric pair, including
+multiple metrics on one field. The external upstream implementation instead uses
+the number of required fields; the 200 published task configurations have one
+metric per field, so this distinction affects extended configurations only.
+
+Key alignment, including exact-match key columns, still calls the configured
+judge with the original prompts. The verifier accepts `OPENAI_API_KEY` and
+`OPENAI_BASE_URL`, with the source's `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`/`ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL`
+fallback. `WIDESEARCH_EVAL_MODEL` and `WIDESEARCH_EVAL_MAX_TOKENS` retain their
+source defaults. Missing judge credentials, incomplete replies, duplicate JSON
+keys, invalid mappings, or omitted/nonbinary item decisions produce
+`infra_error` with minimum reward, preserving any native report for diagnosis.
+Valid unmatched mappings and zero decisions remain scored results.
+
+Missing or empty candidate tables score zero. Missing trusted files are
+infrastructure errors; malformed configurations and empty trusted tables are
+invalid tasks. Legitimate blank cells and original duplicate reference keys are
+preserved. The wrapper observes the source's actual dtype conversion and
+preprocessing boundaries: newly ambiguous candidate keys score zero, ambiguous
+trusted keys invalidate the task, and judge-induced row collisions are
+infrastructure errors. It does not silently deduplicate aligned rows.
+
+Generation requires the Harbor verifyit dispatcher and shared source-runtime
+helper. The generated image pins verifyit revision
+`a0861089947096aabe456ca4308ca46b1b001d7c`; deployment needs that revision to be
+available. Local validation uses its recorded wheel. Evidence from frozen source
+tables and a local judge fixture establishes scorer/runtime behavior, not live
+judge quality or trajectory-archive parity.
